  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run it in a browser, so the rendering is unverified and I haven't run `vite build`.\n\n- **Island:** the terrain is a flat-shaded height field with its own vertices and normal for each triangle. It has per-face colours (sand, two greens, rock). About 16 trees and 14 rocks are scattered on it as instanced cones, cylinders and boxes.\n- **Water:** a 300 m custom-shader mesh with animated vertex waves and faceted normals. It has a shallow/deep tint, fresnel reflection of the sky, a sun or moon glint, a foam ring that pulses along the shore, and a fade to the horizon colour with distance. The sun direction and day amount are passed in as uniforms each frame.\n- **Day/night:** a full 24 h cycle runs in 20 s, starting at 9:00. The Preetham sky (with stars) follows the sun. The sun and moon lights move on arcs, and the sun's intensity and colour change with its height. The hemisphere fill is dimmed and tinted at night but never goes to zero, so the scene is never black.\n- **Camera:** it orbits the island at radius 38 and height 16, looking at the island centre, and it frames the whole island.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set after `app.ready()` plus one `requestAnimationFrame`.\n\nThree calls are optional in the engine's types, so I used optional calls (`?.`). If a build doesn't provide them, that part silently does nothing:\n- `setLight` changes the light colours and intensities.\n- `setUniform` drives the water.\n- `app.camera?.setPose` drives the orbit.\n\nIf `setLight` is missing, the lights stay at their starting intensities. If the other two are missing, the water and orbit freeze.\n\n",
